{"title":"Meter","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>meter</b> (abbreviated m) is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Syst%C3%A8me_international\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Système international\">metric</a> unit for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distance\" title=\"Distance\">distance</a>.\n</p><p>It was one of the first metric units and was originally defined to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5caaee9cdacbefdefff7ada6df927e620ede60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{10,000,000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"95\" height=\"42\" /> times the distance from the North Pole to the Equator along a meridian across France. To find the exact length, several surveyors started from the northernmost point of France straight down to the southernmost point, and then calculated how much the Earth they've traveled. Right now, it is defined by setting the speed of light, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495dd57efe8f9f89b069f46ea367f4e47ff5a4b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$299,792,458 m/s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" /> using the definition of the second.\n</p><p>1 meter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbc54ef8feabfc5d0a2329f0cfbd10af8a6a809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\approx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" /> 1.0936133 yards\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Meter&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distance\" title=\"Distance\">Distance</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Syst%C3%A8me_international\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Système international\">Système international</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Meter&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018095428\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 31/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 256/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 725/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.200      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.200      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5949:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018095428 and revision id 240104. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}